college|REVIEW: Further/higher/specialist education avoids claiming a single national degree level. The Vietnamese gloss offers context-dependent choices; the example uses a plausible local college but the regional institution boundary remains unresolved.
extent|PASS: Degree and range are illustrated by assessing storm damage after daylight, with no invented measurement. Full extent and to some extent are reusable constructions; the Vietnamese preserves the delayed knowledge.
maths|PASS: Number, shape and relationship coverage is appropriate for the subject noun. British maths and American math are spelling guidance, not identity claims; singular agreement and the folding-symmetry example are checked.
reassure|PASS: The guide's statement reduces concern without claiming that reassurance guarantees truth. Someone that and about complements are distinguished; catching the ferry is naturally rendered by kịp chuyến phà.
terrible|PASS: Strong negative evaluation covers an unpleasant microphone sound without asserting a medical condition. Vietnamese rất khó chịu is suitable for noise; at an activity is separate reusable grammar guidance.
